WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.660
Here at VisualPolitik, we love talking about
Asia, you know probably know that by now,

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:05.660
right?

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:08.881
And we like it because we are certain that
this region has a lot to contribute to the

00:00:08.881 --> 00:00:12.879
improvement of our world.

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:16.040
However, not everything is as good as it sounds.

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:21.100
In Asia while we can certainly see plenty
of light, there are also lots of shadows...

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:25.929
And the largest shadow is that, without any
doubt, that the area has become a huge powder

00:00:25.929 --> 00:00:27.510
keg, ready to blow.

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:31.330
On the one hand, this area is spending more
and more in weapons.

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:36.570
&nbsp;In fact, it is expected that, by 2020, the
region will account for more than 30% of all

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:38.710
the world's military spending.

00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:44.980
And, on top of that, it is also becoming a
chessboard for geopolitics.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:49.890
China and India are big, emergent powers,
and with time they are demanding a larger

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:51.960
and larger international influence.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:57.790
Putin's Russia has started to feel concerned
by the Pacific and so has the United States…

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:01.670
Meaning, this area is extremely important.

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:06.530
On the other hand, there are many disagreements
among the different countries in this region,

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:11.400
and it seems that lately they have been looking
for any reason to start a fight.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:14.780
&nbsp;
We can find all kinds of conflicts here: economic,

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:16.280
territorial, historical…

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:19.460
China's conflict with Vietnam here, with Japan
over there…

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:23.420
And then there is India; the situation of
Taiwan; and the problems between Japan and

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:24.420
Russia.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:26.910
Not forgetting the situation in Korea…

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:29.170
The list just grows longer and longer...

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:33.770
We’re going to talk about many of these,
but today we are going to focus on the sleeping

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:35.220
giant…

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:36.670
Japan.

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:42.659
THE TWO NIGHTMARES OF JAPAN
&nbsp;

00:01:42.659 --> 00:01:45.240
Japan is the world's third largest economy.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:50.120
Despite that, this country has had a modest
role in international politics in the last

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:51.120
few decades.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:57.290
However, the situation is changing, particularly
for two reasons: China and North Korea.

00:01:57.290 --> 00:02:00.420
First, there is the emergence of China as
a superpower.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:03.080
But why does Japan care about that?

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:08.410
Well, basically because the emergence of China
has led to a setback in Japan's regional influence.

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:10.479
&nbsp;
Further, both countries maintain a bitter

00:02:10.479 --> 00:02:14.410
conflict over a small archipelago known as
the Senkaku Islands.

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:20.190
“The Senkaku Islands are abandoned, but
they are still a key area in the fishing industry,

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:26.750
they hold large deposits of petrol and gas,
and they also are strategic in sea trade”)

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:31.030
Well, take a look at this chart to see how
the military budget of both countries has

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:32.500
evolved in the last few years.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:38.870
It will give you a better understanding of
Japan’s concern about China’s emergence.

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:43.780
Second, and more recently, there is is North
Korea.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:48.730
Pyongyang, dear viewer, has been obsessed
for the last 20 years, about developing unconventional

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:52.290
war capacities, these mainly being its nuclear
capability.

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:57.940
For now, Korea has managed to create an atomic
bomb of 30 kilotons, which is comparable to

00:02:57.940 --> 00:02:59.670
twice the bomb of that was used on Hiroshima.

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:04.720
They have also succeeded in making ballistic
missiles which can reach not only South Korea,

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:06.750
but also Japan.

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:13.599
In March 2017, North Korea launched 4 ballistic
missiles against Japan.

00:03:13.599 --> 00:03:19.890
It was somehow successful and 3 out of 4 of
them reached Japanese waters, less than 200

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:21.550
miles from the coast.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:26.830
Well, all of this is producing a real psychosis
in Japan:

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:30.670
The Japanese government itself has started
to conduct evacuation drills in the event

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:36.590
of a hypothetical attack and has even distributed
a detailed guide to explain how Japanese citizens

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:39.300
should respond to a North Korean nuclear attack.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:41.810
&nbsp;
Tokyo says that people should have about 10

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:44.620
minutes to react, but that might be an overestimation...

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:50.020
“A missile may not be detected as soon as
it leaves the launch pad.

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:55.950
Depending on the case, the warnings and alarms
might only sound four or five minutes before

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:57.130
a missile arrives.”

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:58.169
Osaka Mayor Hirofumi Yoshimura - JAPAN TIMES
&nbsp;

00:03:58.169 --> 00:04:02.209
With all this going on, we shouldn't be surprised
to find out Japan is acquiring many nuclear

00:04:02.209 --> 00:04:07.090
shelters and equipment for purifying the air
which are designed to fight radiation as well

00:04:07.090 --> 00:04:08.390
as poisonous gas.

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:14.290
“Shinzo Abe, the Japanese Prime Minister
has confirmed North Korea also has the ability

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:16.549
to launch sarin gas missiles” Japan Times

00:04:16.549 --> 00:04:21.349
So, ignoring whether the North Korean threat
is real or not, the reality is that China

00:04:21.349 --> 00:04:25.430
and North Korea are perceived as being significant
threats by Tokyo.

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:29.879
But… before explaining how the country is
planning to fight these threats, let’s have

00:04:29.879 --> 00:04:36.710
a look at what has been the foundation of
their defense policy in the last few decades.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:41.319
JAPAN, A PACIFIST COUNTRY
&nbsp;

00:04:41.319 --> 00:04:45.740
As you all know, Japan was one of the countries
which lost WWII.

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:51.319
As a consequence of this defeat, the country
had to to establish a constitution in 1947,

00:04:51.319 --> 00:04:54.319
which is still in force today.

00:04:54.319 --> 00:04:59.069
In this constitution it states that war and
the use of the force is not be be used unless

00:04:59.069 --> 00:05:00.619
in self-defence.

00:05:00.619 --> 00:05:06.990
“Aspiring sincerely to an international
peace based on justice and order, the Japanese

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:11.979
people forever renounce war as a sovereign
right of the nation […] In order to accomplish

00:05:11.979 --> 00:05:17.729
the aim of the preceding paragraph, land,
sea, and air forces, as well as other war

00:05:17.729 --> 00:05:21.099
potential, will never be maintained”.

00:05:21.099 --> 00:05:25.360
Article 9 of the Japanese Constitution
This means that at first the idea was that

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:27.419
Japan couldn't even have an army.

00:05:27.419 --> 00:05:30.659
The country's protection was the responsibility
of the US...

00:05:30.659 --> 00:05:35.870
However, the Korean War and the tension suffered
during the years of the Cold War changed everything:

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:40.680
all of a sudden both Tokyo as well as Washington
understood it was essential to form a support

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:43.710
force for the American Army in case Japan
needed defence.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:47.940
And that is how the Japanese Self-Defence
Forces were born.

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:51.449
An army whose only possible purpose is defence.

00:05:51.449 --> 00:05:56.910
But one thing is true, formally, the US still
takes care of Japan's protection and keeps

00:05:56.910 --> 00:06:01.830
&nbsp;more than 40,000 soldiers deployed in the
country, and also maintains some its largest

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:04.029
military bases in Japan.

00:06:04.029 --> 00:06:07.969
This is a force which, by the way, is co-financed
by the government of Japan itself...

00:06:07.969 --> 00:06:12.349
We could even say that Japan is the largest
spearhead of the US in Asia.

00:06:12.349 --> 00:06:16.740
However, the new threats Japan perceives in
the region, from China and North Korea have

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:19.589
caused Japan to no longer be satisfied with
this protection.

00:06:19.589 --> 00:06:25.690
So, the question now is, how is Japan responding
to these threats?

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:28.979
ABE´S NEW DIPLOMACY

00:06:28.979 --> 00:06:34.879
To begin with, the Japanese Prime Minister,
Shinzo Abe has started an unusual diplomatic

00:06:34.879 --> 00:06:37.439
race to work against the growing influence
of China.

00:06:37.439 --> 00:06:41.569
For now, he has managed to improve the country’s
relations with South Korea, to strengthen

00:06:41.569 --> 00:06:46.339
its bonds with the US, and even bridge the
gap existing with Putin’s Russia.

00:06:46.339 --> 00:06:51.869
Japan maintains an intense dispute over the
sovereignty of a small archipelago known as

00:06:51.869 --> 00:06:55.719
the Kuril Islands which are now under Russian
sovereignty.

00:06:55.719 --> 00:07:00.669
In fact, the diplomacy Abe has started is
so intense the country is now competing with

00:07:00.669 --> 00:07:02.249
China in Africa.

00:07:02.249 --> 00:07:06.039
(“Japan and China compete for African markets”
East Asia Forum)

00:07:06.039 --> 00:07:10.240
And, as a curious fact, Shinzo Abe was also
the first international leader to meet with

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:15.369
Trump in the famous residence the American
president owns in Florida.

00:07:15.369 --> 00:07:17.360
&nbsp;
It seems like, after this encounter, Abe managed

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:21.509
to win over the President and make him forget
all the attacks he made against Japan when

00:07:21.509 --> 00:07:23.769
he was still a candidate for the Presidency.

00:07:23.769 --> 00:07:26.259
&nbsp;
Because, one thing is true, Trump complained

00:07:26.259 --> 00:07:29.589
quite a lot about Japan… but things can
change.

00:07:29.589 --> 00:07:35.330
(“We are committed to the security of Japan
and all areas under its administrative control.

00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:39.360
(..) The friendship between our two peoples
runs very, very deep.”

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:40.399
Donald Trump.)

00:07:40.399 --> 00:07:44.580
But of course, diplomacy is not always enough…

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:47.830
Japan’s Rearming?

00:07:47.830 --> 00:07:52.449
And so, we finally reach the key point.

00:07:52.449 --> 00:07:56.830
The Japan Self-Defence Forces are often thought
of as some sort of small band of men…

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:59.449
But, really, nothing is further from the truth.

00:07:59.449 --> 00:08:04.709
The Japanese army is larger than the army
of France and the UK combined!

00:08:04.709 --> 00:08:10.430
It is true that, given their name, we may
not think they are important, but the abilities

00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:14.339
and capacity of this strange army are impressive.

00:08:14.339 --> 00:08:16.169
&nbsp;
For many analysts, they are still the best

00:08:16.169 --> 00:08:17.629
army in Asia…

00:08:17.629 --> 00:08:20.499
Although China certainly competes for that
top spot.

00:08:20.499 --> 00:08:25.360
And look, Japan´s investment in defense is
quite low, at less than 1% of its GDP, but

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:27.629
that is still a LOT of money!

00:08:27.629 --> 00:08:33.050
Take a look at this: in 2016, Japan was the
country with the 7th highest spendon defence.

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:38.550
In 2017, the government will give the forces
the largest budget in its history, more than

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:42.430
5 trillion yens, which is around 45 US billion
dollar.

00:08:42.430 --> 00:08:46.850
And, of course, such a quantity in such a
small and, by the way, very well trained army,

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:50.660
is enough for them to acquire some of the
most modern systems available...

00:08:50.660 --> 00:08:55.960
Like the F35; the best American drones; the
Izumo class aircraft carriers or even the

00:08:55.960 --> 00:08:59.740
new fifth generation fighter jet from (which
Mitsubishi is developing).

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:04.350
“Japan reveals the prototype of its last
furtive fighters” RT

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:09.000
The thing is that, since Abe became Prime
Minister in 2012, he has had the clear idea

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:13.640
of leaving behind the pacifist character set
by the Japanese constitution.

00:09:13.640 --> 00:09:14.750
And this has happened:

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:19.880
In 2014, the Japanese government decided to
stop all restrictions on the export of warfare

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:23.720
material, with the goal of starting a new
Japanese military industry.

00:09:23.720 --> 00:09:29.270
A bit later, in 2015, Abe also led a reform
so that the Self-Defence Forces could operate

00:09:29.270 --> 00:09:32.152
abroad and today they even have a military
base in Djibouti.

00:09:32.152 --> 00:09:39.190
And, of course, the military budget has increased
again after many years of budget cuts.

00:09:39.190 --> 00:09:40.370
But, not only this…

00:09:40.370 --> 00:09:44.010
They are even thinking about changing the
constitution.

00:09:44.010 --> 00:09:51.000
(“The radical military shift of Japan echoes
the ghosts of World War II”.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:52.000
BBC)

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:54.200
So, What do you think?

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:56.650
Should Japan leave its pacifism aside?

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:58.630
Should Japan give in to Beijing?

00:09:58.630 --> 00:10:02.410
Which country seems like a better ally for
you: Japan or China?

